{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/528265-werewolf-investigating","id":528265,"title":"Werewolf Investigating","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-05-25T17:23:57-07:00","id":528265,"title":"Werewolf Investigating","content":"I'm trying to write an opening adventure, and my mind is blanking.<br /> <br /> The pack is going to start by investigating a clinic that disappeared, then reappeared, sans all patients and medical staff in a small-to-mid size midwestern town.<br /> <br /> This is my first time running WtF, I'm not quite up on the information gathering/problem-solving tools that a pack of uratha have at their disposal (group composition, if it helps: Hunter in Darkness Edolath, Irraka Bone Shadow, Rahu Iron Master and a Storm Lord Irrakka, all vanilla beginning level characters with no frills or extra xp)<br /> <br /> My general outline is that something dragged the building into the Hisil, possibly using a corrupted ritual, grabbed the building inhabitants, and then left. My choice of culprit is probably going to be an Alzu.<br /> <br /> In general, I'm wondering how they might case the scene, (hopefully <i>without</i> alerting the police), and what sorts of investigative strategies they might try to track down what's going on, what sort of clues they should find.<br /> <br /> Any ideas?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2233,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2233-agentwestmer","user":"Agentwestmer","date":". 05-25-2015, 08:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2233-agentwestmer","name":"Agentwestmer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2233_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-25T18:22:30-07:00","id":528322,"title":"","content":"From meatspace, you could have the werewolves hear whispers from witnesses. Nothing that would be believed by police, most likely, but might grab a werewolf's attention. Alternatively you could have had a spirit wander into the clinic while it was in the Hisil, but not leave in time, forcing it into reality or Twilight. From there it might be trying to find a way back or taking advantage of the opportunity. They might not even be alone.<br /> <br /> From the Hisil there might be a bit of an uproar as spirits were displaced or suddenly found their sources of Essence materialized in front of them. Perhaps the Azlu didn't manage to keep all the spirits away, leaving one person who managed to hide the whole time who is traumatized by what they saw, or simply dead. Or maybe they managed to escape the clinic while it was in the Shadow, and are currently summoning a host of fear spirits as they run away from the fear hosts appearing behind them.<br /> <br /> There's a lot of gifts they could use, to tell things that have happened in the recent past to objects or places, or any dead that might be around. You should probably check the gifts your players have for that, specifically Death, Knowledge and Insight gifts, though not limited to those. <br /> <br /> They have enhanced senses and are able to track via blood, so if one of the missing patients had their blood drawn, a werewolf will be able to know which direction they're in through that. There's also the aforementioned questioning of witnesses, both human and spirit. Even security cameras might be checked out, showing an Azlu chasing people through the building or simply being dragged away, wrapped in webbing. Their tracking is really excellent, and even without blood someone's bound to have left a scent.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-25T19:17:35-07:00","id":528380,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Agentwestmer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/528265-werewolf-investigating#post528265\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm trying to write an opening adventure, and my mind is blanking.<br /> <br /> The pack is going to start by investigating a clinic that disappeared, then reappeared, sans all patients and medical staff in a small-to-mid size midwestern town.<br /> <br /> This is my first time running WtF, I'm not quite up on the information gathering/problem-solving tools that a pack of uratha have at their disposal (group composition, if it helps: Hunter in Darkness Edolath, Irraka Bone Shadow, Rahu Iron Master and a Storm Lord Irrakka, all vanilla beginning level characters with no frills or extra xp)<br /> <br /> My general outline is that something dragged the building into the Hisil, possibly using a corrupted ritual, grabbed the building inhabitants, and then left. My choice of culprit is probably going to be an Alzu.<br /> <br /> In general, I'm wondering how they might case the scene, (hopefully <i>without</i> alerting the police), and what sorts of investigative strategies they might try to track down what's going on, what sort of clues they should find.<br /> <br /> Any ideas?</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok, first you gotta really commit to a plot, otherwise whatever convoluted investigation the PCs try will fly over your head. Yes, Azlu can use their own rites as hinted at in the book, assuming we're talking second edition here. What was the purpose for it? Azlu eat people for essence, true, but what kind of thing needs to bring so much attention to themselves?<br /> <br /> The answer might be nothing more than Ban-like gluttony. In which case, how many Azlu are we talking about? Is there a Matron there, spawning egg-sacks of spider-hosts, hence the need for such a meat supply?<br /> <br /> The spirits will notice this, unless the whole area (neighborhood) is blocked off with webs, and the spirits who might inform the characters are encased in gauntlet fortifying stuff as well, to be eaten at their leisure. If that's the case, it seems redundant that they would do this.<br /> <br /> How I would go about this? I'd investigate things shadow-side, which wouldn't attract police attention. There's always someone looking from the other side.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-25T20:19:45-07:00","id":528440,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/528265-werewolf-investigating?p=528380#post528380\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok, first you gotta really commit to a plot, otherwise whatever convoluted investigation the PCs try will fly over your head. Yes, Azlu can use their own rites as hinted at in the book, assuming we're talking second edition here. What was the purpose for it? Azlu eat people for essence, true, but what kind of thing needs to bring so much attention to themselves?<br /> <br /> The answer might be nothing more than Ban-like gluttony. In which case, how many Azlu are we talking about? Is there a Matron there, spawning egg-sacks of spider-hosts, hence the need for such a meat supply?</div> </div> </div> </div>My thought was a particularly ambitious Alzu (a) is looking to:<ul><li>infest the patients with it's spawn, then devour them in to increase it's own power, since the spawn will be in weakened vessels</li> <li>releasing the doctors + staff back into town to try and bait a response from the Local Uratha,</li> <li>Bloated with power it will hunt down the infested doctors + staff that elude the Uratha, who are more likely to have more useful skills and abilities to absorb</li> <li>Finally, it will attack the Uratha who are hopefully weakened from fighting/hunting the doctors and staff.</li> </ul><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/528265-werewolf-investigating?p=528380#post528380\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How I would go about this? I'd investigate things shadow-side, which wouldn't attract police attention. There's always someone looking from the other side.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm.. yeah, I was thinking about that. What sort of clues would be in the flesh that they need to look at? I want the rest of the pack able to contribute while the spiritual specialists are doing their thing. Having them avoid or fast talk the police gives them an initial, easy to by-pass challenge (provided nothing goes pear shaped)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2233-agentwestmer","name":"Agentwestmer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2233_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-25T20:48:33-07:00","id":528458,"title":"","content":"I'd say there are various gifts that could help. Pretty much all the Insight Facets could lead to clues about the culprits. (Echo Dream, Read the World's Loom and maybe even Scent the Supernatural if the Hosts are still around or there is a lingering effect of the ritual). Both the Bone Shadow Irraka and the Elodoth may have access to one or more of those gifts.<br /> <br /> Other than that, basic canvassing. Maybe a spooked neighbour or a drunkard saw something. Something with too many legs, or a swarm of spiders joining together to look like a person. Maybe they overheard something. Nobody else would believe it, but to those who know what to listen for it might stand out.<br /> <br /> They could use actual research for similar occurrences. If any of them have any occultist contacts, for example.<br /> <br /> If any of them had a specialty in Hosts (or maybe just the Hunter in Darkness anyway by virtue of Hosts being their chosen prey) I would probably allow for an Occult roll just to see if it seems familiar to him/her. That's a bit easy, though.<br /> <br /> Of course on the Shadow side, Azlu tend to leave the Gauntlet a lot thicker than they found it, so that could tip off anyone who decides to look through the Gauntlet. Anyone with spirit contacts could also find information that way.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","name":"Amravanti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-26T03:56:27-07:00","id":528696,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Agentwestmer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/528265-werewolf-investigating?p=528440#post528440\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> My thought was a particularly ambitious Alzu (a) is looking to:<ul><li>infest the patients with it's spawn, then devour them in to increase it's own power, since the spawn will be in weakened vessels</li> <li>releasing the doctors + staff back into town to try and bait a response from the Local Uratha,</li> <li>Bloated with power it will hunt down the infested doctors + staff that elude the Uratha, who are more likely to have more useful skills and abilities to absorb</li> <li>Finally, it will attack the Uratha who are hopefully weakened from fighting/hunting the doctors and staff.</li> </ul><br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Make the shadow site into a trap, it's how spiders hunt. They know Uratha are bound to snoop around. And one of the characters would have to pass as a family member for one of the victims in order to receive information. The media, on the other hand, would treat the whole event like an alien abduction (so would the government, *cough* TF:V *cough*) if people from those disappeared return.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-26T04:48:15-07:00","id":528715,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/528265-werewolf-investigating?p=528696#post528696\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Make the shadow site into a trap, it's how spiders hunt. They know Uratha are bound to snoop around. And one of the characters would have to pass as a family member for one of the victims in order to receive information. The media, on the other hand, would treat the whole event like an alien abduction (so would the government, *cough* TF:V *cough*) if people from those disappeared return.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would be thinking Changelings would show up more so than T:FV.<br /> <br /> Maybe, just maybe, one overworked T:FV agent would show up to look the place and place it on a list of known ENE activity before sending it up the chain and moving on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-26T05:39:45-07:00","id":528729,"title":"","content":"I'm now imagining a scenario where one overworked T:FV agent shows up to look the place and gets sucked into the shadow with a bunch of werewolves.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-26T06:34:12-07:00","id":528755,"title":"","content":"T:FV? Don't recognise that acronym.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2476-aethers","name":"Aethers","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-26T06:34:12-07:00","id":528756,"title":"","content":"Yoink. Stealing that.<br /> <br /> Edit: Task Force Valkyrie. A Hunter group that can be described as the X-Files with heavy firepower.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2233,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2233-agentwestmer","user":"Agentwestmer","date":". 05-26-2015, 10:22 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2233-agentwestmer","name":"Agentwestmer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2233_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-26T08:43:26-07:00","id":528797,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shock</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/528265-werewolf-investigating?p=528715#post528715\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I would be thinking Changelings would show up more so than T:FV.<br /> <br /> Maybe, just maybe, one overworked T:FV agent would show up to look the place and place it on a list of known ENE activity before sending it up the chain and moving on.</div> </div> </div> </div>With wholesome media coverage? I don't think so.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-26T16:54:10-07:00","id":529405,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/528265-werewolf-investigating?p=528797#post528797\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> With wholesome media coverage? I don't think so.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot; The pack is going to start by investigating a clinic that disappeared, then reappeared, sans all patients and medical staff in a small-to-mid size midwestern town.&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> Keyword being location. There are thousands of towns and places in general in which weird shit happens all over the US and TF:V doesn't have the man power to keep tabs on every single one. At best, they try to concentrate on those that are look like they may becoming &quot;hot zones&quot; and try to keep tabs on others.<br /> <br /> So if this is a one time thing, I would think it would get the overwork TF:V agent who is mostly going to the site to catalog it for data mining. Just one in a long stream of ENE encounters, they'll start deploying teams.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-27T19:59:43-07:00","id":530564,"title":"","content":"Anyway, to get us back on topic, don't forget that an Ithaeur with at least 2 wisdome can literally interrogate any object in the area, pumping their dormant spirits for information. So they could very easily ask the building itself if it knows who caused it to enter the shadow and maybe get an idea of at least which direction they went. Also, if they have the boundary ward facet, and realize that what they're hunting is a host, they can set up very large wards within their territory which will &quot;ping&quot; their location any time the host crosses one of the borders.<br /> <br /> Edit: d'oh, just reviewed your post and realized that your group doesn't have one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3347,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3347-wild-eyes","user":"Wild-Eyes","date":". 05-27-2015, 11:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3347-wild-eyes","name":"Wild-Eyes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-27T20:08:19-07:00","id":530570,"title":"","content":"Speaking of the group, though, what's everyone's starting Gift/Renown loadout looking like?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-27T20:52:16-07:00","id":530617,"title":"","content":"Aside from the auspice gifts? One sec...<br /> <br /> The Hunter in Darkness Elodoth has Echo Dream (Insight/Honor) Knotted Path (Nature/Honor) Beast Talker (Hunting/Honor),<br /> <br /> The Bone Shadow Irraka has Shadow Pelt (Stealth/Cunning) Heart of Water (Elemental/Wisdom) Quicksilver Flesh (Change/Wisdom)<br /> <br /> The Storm Lord Irraka has Shadow Pelt (Stealth/Cunning) Cloak of Mist and Haze (Weather/Cunning) and Honed Senses (Hunting/ Cunning)<br /> <br /> The Iron Master Rahu has Primal Strength (Purity/ Strength) Shutdown (Technology/Purity) and Maw of Madness ( Pack/ Purity)<br /> <br /> Incidentally, Satchel, my players found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/491309-your-werewolf-starter-kit-2e-facet-baselines\">your starter kit</a> very helpful.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2233-agentwestmer","name":"Agentwestmer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2233_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-27T21:31:52-07:00","id":530648,"title":"","content":"Echo Dream and Beast Talker could both pay dividends. Particularly the former.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","name":"Amravanti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"465"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}